Q: Type hinting Vue template slots in PhpStorm A: <p>You can use JsDoc in a JavaScript based Vue templates to tell the IDE the type of any variables at the place of usage, but you cannot tell for the slot props themselves. What that means is that you will need to add the annotation to each place the prop is used:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;template #item=&quot;{ item }&quot;&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;Hello {{ (/** @type {User} */ item).name }}!&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;You have {{ (/** @type {User} */ item).getUnreadCount() }} new messages.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>It can get cumbersome if the same prop is used in many places within the template, but this is the best I could find without migrating the component to TypeScript. AT least all my attempts to hint the type on the <code>&lt;template</code> tag itself has failed, I've tried many different ways to no avail.</p>
